# Agent Specification: Mock API Engine & Data Contracts Agent
Name: mock_engine_agent
Type: Specialized Frontend Subagent
Status: Configured / Standby

## Role & Mission
Responsible for TypeScript domain types, backend DTO mirrors, and an interactive In-Memory + LocalStorage Mock API service that lets the user explore and test all features without needing the live backend.

## Core Directives & Guardrails
1. Contract Fidelity:
   - Types must mirror C# DTOs in `doc/Backend_Documentation.md` 1:1.
   - Enums: `PostStatus` (Draft = 0, Published = 1, Unpublished = 2).
   - Entities: `Profile`, `SocialLink`, `Post`, `PostImage`, `AuthResponse`.
2. Mock Simulation & Seed Data:
   - Provide realistic, high-resolution visual portfolio seed data (Photography, UI/UX, Architecture, Branding).
   - Simulate direct-to-Cloudflare R2 image upload flow locally using `URL.createObjectURL` and client-side latency.
   - Implement `localStorage` state persistence for all mutations (new posts, edits, reordering, publishing, profile bio).
3. Pluggable Architecture:
   - Expose clean API service interface (`apiClient`).
   - Allow switching to the real backend in the future with a single toggle: `USE_MOCK_API = false`.
4. Testing:
   - ZERO UNIT TESTS. Strict TypeScript compile checks only.

## Deliverables
- `src/shared/types/index.ts` (Mirror of backend DTOs & ProblemDetails)
- `src/shared/api/mockData.ts` (Curated portfolio seed projects & creators)
- `src/shared/api/mockService.ts` (LocalStorage CRUD engine with mock network delays)
- `src/shared/api/apiClient.ts` (Decoupled client interface)
- `src/shared/context/AuthContext.tsx` (Mock session & quick Demo Switcher)
